          "prompt": "MANDATORY: a 2 by 2 GRID of exactly four separate orthographic views of the SAME object: TOP-LEFT = FRONT view; TOP-RIGHT = LEFT side view (object turned so its front points to the LEFT edge of the image); BOTTOM-LEFT = BACK view; BOTTOM-RIGHT = RIGHT side view (object turned so its front points to the RIGHT edge of the image). Each view seen straight on from slightly above (about 15 degrees) so the top surface is just visible, same scale in all four, wide empty gaps between the views, every view complete and not cropped. Plain flat light neutral grey background (#D6D6D6). No floor, no ground shadow, no text, no labels, no frames, no perspective, no extra objects. No fire, no smoke, no sparks, no lava, no glow halo: hot cracks, ember beds, flame tips and lantern glass are painted only as flat opaque bright orange-yellow colour areas.\n\nREFERENCE: the attached image is a crop of our approved scene concept. Redraw ONLY the square stone pier from it as a standalone game asset, keeping its shapes, proportions, materials and colours, simplified as described below; ignore everything else in the crop.\n\nSTYLE: stylized hand-painted 3D game environment asset: thick chunky silhouette that still reads as a solid black shape, broad clean faceted planes, two or three dominant colour blocks (dark violet-grey basalt, warm aged bronze, deep vermilion lacquer), soft painted gradients, a few medium-size ornaments, sparse wear, soot-darkened edges. No photorealism, no micro-grain, no fine brick seams, no dense cracks, no tiny carvings, no harsh highlights. Anything at ground level is basalt, stone or cast iron; timber only high up on buildings.\n\nOBJECT (14m wide x 8m tall x 14m deep): A massive square pier of big dark violet-grey basalt blocks, 14m wide and 6m tall with slightly rounded corners and a plain stone top edge; on its flat top, at the back centre, a stepped square plinth two steps high (2m) that is EMPTY (it will carry a giant cauldron). On the FRONT face: a big round cast bronze emblem disc in the centre and two long vermilion banners with gold flame emblems hanging flat on either side of it. Four heavy black iron mooring rings bolted to the top edge at the corners. PROPORTIONS: all four views about 1.75 times as wide as tall.",
